Hello All,

In general when making reference to something it is best to use the complet=
e name to avoid confusion.

For instance, when referring to the material out of which some of the large=
r threaded fittings are made that are found in our DI price sheets, it is b=
est not to refer to them in the way of shorthand as made of =93malleable=94=
.  Use the full name =93malleable iron=94.

Malleable is a characteristic of certain metals not a material itself.

We use malleable iron fittings for certain configurations and certain sizes=
 because ductile iron thread fittings are not available.

Malleable iron and ductile iron are both irons that have high ductility and=
 high strength relative to cast iron.  They achieve these properties by dif=
ferent methods in the production process.

John

--_000_9B7E2735CEC37E4D9137A9548F21D78372545FCA07MAIL_
